{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem showed him all the land</b> — all the land of Israel that is across the Jordan. And afterward Scripture mentions that He showed him Gilead as far as Dan. Now Moses was in the portion of Reuben, and half the hill country of Gilead with its cities belonged to the children of Reuben and half to Manasseh; therefore its meaning is from Gilead as far as Dan. Or perhaps Gilead was in Lebanon, in the land of Israel, as it is written (Jeremiah 22:6), \"Are you to me Gilead, the head of Lebanon?\" And He mentioned <b>as far as Dan</b>, for it is the end of the boundary of the land of Israel, as it is written (II Samuel 24:2), \"Go about now through all the tribes of Israel, from Dan to Beersheba.\" And He mentioned Ephraim and Manasseh, for they were in the north of the land of Israel, and the land of Judah, which is in the south, as it is written (Joshua 18:5), \"Judah shall stand by their border on the south, and the house of Joseph shall stand by their border on the north,\" and Judah took all the southern part of the land of Israel, from the Jordan to the sea, and Dan took in the northwest. And He mentioned Naphtali, which adjoins Judah from the east (Joshua 19:34). And He did not mention Asher and Issachar, for they were within Ephraim and Manasseh, as it is written (Joshua 17:10), \"And they meet with Asher from the north and with Issachar from the east.\" And He did not mention Simeon, for the inheritance of Simeon was from the portion of the children of Judah (Joshua 19:1). And He did not mention Benjamin, for the border of their lot was between the children of Judah and the children of Joseph, who are mentioned adjacent to them. And He mentioned \"as far as the hinder sea\" for Zebulun, which was on the seacoast, or perhaps it was included in the Negev and the valley. And He mentions the plain of Jericho because it is a deep valley and was not visible from the top of the mountain, but He showed it to him by way of a miracle. And the general principle is that He showed him the entire inheritance of Israel, as it is written (Deuteronomy 34:4), \"This is the land which I swore,\" etc. And to our Sages in the Sifrei (Berachah, section 297) there are midrashim in these places that Scripture mentions. And the reason for this vision that He showed him is that the land was full of all good, the glory of all lands, and because it was revealed before Him the great love that Moses our master had for Israel — his joy was increased through the abundance of goodness seen by his eyes:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "In the parenthetical variant marked ס\"א (a different manuscript witness), the text reads: 'and Manasseh and Ephraim, all the north as well, from the Jordan to the sea.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:58.935950047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}